{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dermatoid-brassy-junco","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nAfter repository extraction, `BindingStore` still owns forward/reverse identity transitions, pending/confirmed state, stale reverse cleanup, and immutable numeric-ID moves. These coupled rules need one policy owner and both-index tests.\n\n## Outcome\nCreate the first `BindingLifecycle` slice for bind, confirm, unbind, reverse cleanup, and numeric-ID re-key while the public facade retains all signatures and owns coordination.\n\n## Plan\n1. Start with table-driven failing tests over valid, missing, corrupt, duplicate, and stale forward/reverse combinations.\n2. Move the cohesive identity transition call graph into `binding_lifecycle.py`, operating on repository-owned original dictionaries.\n3. Preserve safety-abort on ambiguous double bind, stale reverse removal, pending/confirmed semantics, immutable numeric-ID re-key, and legacy no-ID behavior.\n4. Delegate existing facade methods without exposing the lifecycle owner or repository to adapters.\n\n## Testing\nReload through the real repository after every transition and assert both indexes plus exact caller-visible outcomes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every valid bind/confirm/unbind transition leaves at most one forward and one matching reverse identity.\n- [ ] Ambiguous double binds safety-abort without guessed deletion.\n- [ ] Stale reverse entries are removed only in the existing permitted cases.\n- [ ] Immutable numeric-ID matches re-key moved issues instead of retiring them.\n- [ ] Legacy records without numeric IDs retain current behavior and facade signatures.\n\n## Out of scope\nAbsence/tombstone/comment policy and rich-emission mutation move to later S2 tasks.","id":"6083-b802-e90a-416e","parent_id":"fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb","priority":1,"tags":["rp02","binding-lifecycle","tdd"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S2 T1 — Extract binding identity transitions"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787027525763725001,"uuid":"6cc63685-5fce-4f91-9ae6-da8150eef994"}